Cross php85 makes phar.phar with the native php.

ext/phar/Makefile.frag runs PHP to generate phar.php and phar.phar and
prefers the sapi/cli/php the build has just linked. In a cross build that
is a target executable: the host shell could not run it ("not executable:
64-bit ELF file"), make ignored the errors, and install stopped with
bin/phar85.phar not installed in DESTDIR. Depend on the native php85 of
the same version as a tool and pass its TOOLBASE path as PHP_EXECUTABLE
and PHP_PHARCMD_EXECUTABLE, which every build-time PHP run in the
Makefile uses. phar.phar stays in the PLIST. Native builds are unchanged.
Applies after php85-cross-build-cc.patch.
Origin: EmberBSD (AI-assisted); upstream status: not submitted.

--- a/lang/php85/Makefile
+++ b/lang/php85/Makefile
@@ -29,6 +29,12 @@
 .  else
 CONFIGURE_ENV+=		BUILD_CC=${NATIVE_CC:Q}
 .  endif
+# ext/phar runs PHP to make phar.php and phar.phar and prefers the
+# sapi/cli/php it has just linked, a target executable in a cross build.
+# Run the native php of the same version in TOOLBASE instead.
+TOOL_DEPENDS+=		${PKGNAME}:../../lang/php85
+MAKE_FLAGS+=		PHP_EXECUTABLE=${TOOLBASE}/bin/php${PHP_VER}
+MAKE_FLAGS+=		PHP_PHARCMD_EXECUTABLE=${TOOLBASE}/bin/php${PHP_VER}
 .endif
 MAKE_ENV+=		INSTALL_ROOT=${DESTDIR}
 
